; Integer-valued options (--head, --tail, --depth, --period-shift,
; --decimal-places, --columns, the column widths, --meta-width, --seed,
; --forecast-years, --prepend-width, --abbrev-len) take a whole decimal
; number that fits in an int (--seed: an unsigned int).  A value that is
; not one is rejected when the option is set, naming the option, instead
; of surfacing "bad lexical cast" or "stoi: no conversion" from wherever
; the value happened to be used, or silently dropping trailing characters
; such as the x in 15x.  The accepted values are pinned in
; option-int-values.test.

2024/01/05 Grocer
    Expenses:Food:Groceries    $10.25
    Assets:Cash

2024/02/05 Diner
    Expenses:Food:Dining       $20.00
    Assets:Cash

2024/03/05 Grocer
    Expenses:Food:Groceries    $30.00
    Assets:Cash

test reg --depth=abc -> 1
__ERROR__
While parsing option '--depth=abc'
Error: Invalid value for --depth: abc
end test

